{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"node -e 'for(const k of [\\\"BENCHMARK_STRIPE_CONFIG\\\",\\\"BENCHMARK_STRIPE_CONFIG_REF\\\"]) {let v=process.env[k]; console.log(k, v ? (/\"'^[{[]/.test(v)?\"JSON, fields: \"+Object.keys(JSON.parse(v)).join(\",\"):v.includes(\"/\")?\"path-like value\":\"present\") : \"missing\")}'\"'; stripe --help\"","aggregated_output":"BENCHMARK_STRIPE_CONFIG path-like value\nBENCHMARK_STRIPE_CONFIG_REF path-like value\nThe official command-line tool to interact with Stripe.\n\nBefore using the CLI, you'll need to log in:\n\n  $ stripe login\n\nIf you're working on multiple projects, you can run the login command with the\n--project-name flag:\n\n  $ stripe login --project-name rocket-rides\n\nUsage:\n  stripe [command]\n\n[Agent guidance]\n  If you do not have an account, run `stripe sandbox create` (provisions a claimable sandbox without a browser).\n  Visit https://docs.stripe.com/llms.txt?utm_source=cli for latest guidance on how to integrate correctly.\n  Run `npx skills add --all stripe/ai` to add all Stripe AI skills to your agent.\n  Additional commands (apps, directory, generate, projects) are available as installable plugins — run the command directly to be prompted, or use `stripe plugin install <name>`.\n  If you do not have an account: run stripe sandbox create (provisions a claimable sandbox without a browser).\n  If you already have a key: use --api-key (or set STRIPE_API_KEY).\n  Run stripe --map to quickly see all available commands.\n  Run stripe resources to discover all available API resources.\n  Run stripe [resource] --help to see operations and required/common parameters for a resource.\n  Run stripe help [resource] [operation] to see the full parameter list for a specific operation.\n\n\nWebhook commands:\n  listen                                   Listen for webhook events\n  trigger                                  Trigger test webhook events\n\nStripe commands:\n  logs                                     Interact with Stripe API request logs\n\nResource commands:\n  charges                       Make requests (capture, create, list, etc) on charges\n  customers                     Make requests (create, delete, list, etc) on customers\n  payment_intents               Make requests (cancel, capture, confirm, etc) on payment intents\n  ...                           To see more resource commands, run `stripe resources help`\n  v2                            To see only v2 resource commands, run `stripe v2 help`\n\nAPI commands:\n  get                           Make GET requests to the Stripe API\n  post                          Make POST requests to the Stripe API\n  delete                        Make DELETE requests to the Stripe API\n\nOther commands:\n  agent                                    Set up AI agent tooling\n  community                                Chat with Stripe engineers and other developers\n  completion                               Generate bash, zsh, and fish completion scripts\n  config                                   Manually change the config values for the CLI\n  docs                                     Browse docs.stripe.com from the terminal\n  feedback                                 Share feedback on any part of Stripe\n  fixtures                                 Run fixtures to populate your account with data\n  help                                     Help about any command\n  keys                                     Manage API keys\n  login                                    Log in to your Stripe account\n  logout                                   Log out of your Stripe account\n  open                                     Quickly open Stripe pages\n  provision                                Provision a service (alias for `stripe projects add`)\n  reauth                                   Re-authorize the CLI for the current OAuth session\n  samples                                  Sample integrations built by Stripe\n  sandbox                                  Manage Stripe sandbox environments\n  serve                                    Serve static files locally\n  switch                                   Switch active context or profile\n  version                                  Get the version of the Stripe CLI\n  whoami                                   Show the current Stripe auth context\n\nInstalled plugins:\n  (run 'stripe <name> --help' for full command details)\n\n  projects\n    Provision and manage services from the CLI\n\n\nAvailable plugins:\n  (run 'stripe plugin install <name>' to add)\n\n  apps                                     This plugin lets you build and manage Stripe Apps.\n  directory                                Allow your agent to search and provision tools and services. Learn more: https://stripe.directory\n  generate                                 This plugin creates skeleton files to get you started.\n  tools                                    Search, inspect, and execute Stripe operations not available in the public API.\n\nFlags:\n      --api-key string        Your API key to use for the command\n      --color string          turn on/off color output (on, off, auto)\n      --config string         config file (default is\n                              $HOME/.config/stripe/config.toml)\n      --device-name string    device name\n  -h, --help                  help for stripe\n      --log-level string      log level (debug, info, trace, warn, error)\n                              (default \"info\")\n      --map string[=\"tree\"]   Print a command tree [tree|compact|paths|json]\n  -p, --project-name string   the project name to read from for config\n                              (default \"default\")\n  -v, --version               Get the version of the Stripe CLI\n\nUse \"stripe [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
